	<div class="page-header">
		<h1>Rottneros Park</h1>
	</div>

	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			Rottneros Park is one of Scandinavia's largest collections of Nordic sculpture, set in
			gardens built around the old Rottneros manor grounds. It's directly inspired by — and
			partly the setting for — Selma Lagerlöf's romantic stories; the manor appears as "Ekeby"
			in <em>Gösta Berlings saga</em>.
		</p>
		<p>
			The mill and manor at Rottneros share a history with <a href="/history">Öjerviks gård</a> —
			both were owned by the Påhlson and Montgomery families in the early 20th century, just a
			few kilometers apart. The park also hosts <strong>Västanå Teater</strong>'s annual summer
			play.
		</p>
		<p>
			Rottneros Park also partners on weddings and celebrations, including formal dinners in its
			"Hall of Mirrors" — see the <a href="/celebrate">Celebrate</a> page for details.
		</p>
	</div>
